---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { NAV, SITE } from '../lib/site';
---
<Base
  title="Security"
  description="Itemized’s security controls for self-hosters (authentication, non-root containers, reverse proxy rate limiting, sandboxed demo mode) and how to report vulnerabilities."
>
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="kicker">Security</p>
      <h1>Defense in depth for self-hosted instances.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        How itemized handles authentication, container privileges, reverse proxies, and responsible vulnerability disclosure.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2>Security controls in itemized</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Authentication &amp; roles:</strong> Supports local password authentication and optional OIDC SSO using Authorization Code flow with PKCE (tested with Authentik, Authelia, Pocket ID, and Keycloak). Accounts use <strong>Admin</strong> and <strong>Member</strong> roles, and <code>OIDC_FORCE=true</code> disables local password login completely.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Non-root container execution:</strong> The container entrypoint ensures <code>/data</code> ownership matches <code>PUID:PGID</code> and drops privileges to run <code>/usr/local/bin/itemized</code> as a non-root user. Explicit non-root <code>--user</code> launches are supported automatically.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Reverse proxy rate limiting:</strong> Set <code>TRUST_PROXY=true</code> when running behind a reverse proxy so rate limiting reads client IPs from <code>X-Forwarded-For</code> / <code>X-Real-IP</code> rather than the proxy address.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>HTTPS for camera access:</strong> Serving itemized over HTTPS protects credentials in transit and satisfies browser security requirements for mobile camera barcode scanning. See <a href={`${NAV.selfHost}#https`}>HTTPS &amp; Reverse Proxy</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Sandboxed public demo mode:</strong> When <code>DEMO_MODE=true</code> is enabled, outbound printer, OIDC, and LLM calls are sandboxed, UPC lookups are rate-limited to 5/min, and sample data resets automatically on <code>DEMO_RESET_INTERVAL</code>.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Reporting a vulnerability</h2>
      <p>
        If you discover a security vulnerability in itemized, please report it privately using <a href={SITE.securityAdvisories}>GitHub Security Advisories</a> rather than opening a public issue.
      </p>
      <p>
        Include steps to reproduce, the affected version or container digest, and any relevant configuration details so the issue can be verified and patched quickly.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
